# Testing

- Use pytest; name files `test_*.py`.
- Mock HTTP with `responses` or `unittest.mock` — do not hit Open-Meteo in unit tests.
- Test observable behavior (cache contents, HTTP status codes) not private implementation details.
- Use a temporary cache path or isolate `data/cache.json` in fixtures when testing fetcher.
- Create the Flask app with `create_app(enable_scheduler=False)` to avoid background jobs in tests.
